{%- comment -%}
  FIXTURE — must PASS the comment-integrity lint.

  Deliberately packed with constructs that a naive implementation would
  false-positive on. Every one of these is legal and must stay quiet:
    - a comment whose body is long English prose (comments are stripped, so
      prose inside one never reaches selector position)
    - a comment containing backticks (same reason)
    - a comment that legitimately ends immediately after a quote character
    - Liquid tags inside the <style> block, including braces
    - @media / @supports headers, which contain words and parentheses
    - long multi-class selectors and attribute selectors

  A false positive here blocks CI on correct code, so this fixture is the
  guard on the guard.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* A perfectly ordinary comment with several English words in a row,
     explaining why this rule exists and what it protects against.
     It even references `.header__wrapper` and `contain: layout` in
     backticks, which is fine — this text is stripped before parsing. */
  .header__desktop {
    height: 70px;
  }

  /* A comment ending right after a quoted word like "this" */
  .footer__title {
    background: transparent;
  }

  {%- if settings.enable_sticky_header %}
  .header--sticky {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
  }
  {%- endif %}

  @media only screen and (max-width: 767px) {
    .announcement__wrapper [data-ticker-frame] {
      height: 24px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
  }

  @supports not (display: grid) {
    .product-grid-item {
      float: left;
    }
  }

  .quick-buy__popover,
  .quick-buy__option-title[data-variant-id] {
    display: none;
  }

  .vrec-product-sticky-bar {
    position: fixed;
    transform: translateY(100%);
  }

  .vrec-product-sticky-bar.is-visible {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
</style>
